  - "Here's why that leaves you so unmoored even when nothing is technically wrong: a transition doesn't just change your circumstances, it dismantles the scaffolding you'd built your days and your sense of self around. Of course you feel wobbly. You're standing in the gap between one structure and the next. That gap is exactly where this work is useful, and you don't have to stand in it alone."
